{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310870,"nonce":"0ak08pf8OnMoFfsg8Dr92F7dErQ=","title":"Apple AMX line COMPLETE (2026-07-14): int8-BNNS closed; Q6-misroute bleed fixed 636ca4d2; f16 shipped daf7d4d5; workspace prealloc 301f5071 ...","message":"**AMX now also covers the plain-F32 `matmulT` path (2026-07-15, commit 8488d48b, BERT Phase 3).**\nBefore, only the Q4_K_M weight path (`rayzor_tensor_matmul_qt_t_f32_threaded`) reached AMX; F32/F16\nweights ran single-threaded NEON. Added `quant::amx_matmul_t_f32` (mirrors `amx_prefill_matmul` but\nkeys the leaked f16 weight cache off a plain-F32 weight pointer — f32→f16, no dequant) and grafted it\ninto `rayzor_tensor_matmul_t_threaded` (the variant the Haxe `matmulT` MIR wrapper routes to — the\nsequential `rayzor_tensor_matmul_t` stays byte-exact F32). Same gate (RZT_AMX_PREFILL + m≥16 +\ncontiguous). MiniLM F32: ~8× on a 40-tok sentence. See [[project_bert_second_architecture]].\n\n\nThe pool-profile / CPU-scheduling work raises ROBUSTNESS, not the compute ceiling.\nThe user explicitly wants these remembered as the bigger levers we have NOT touched:\n\n- **Apple special compute (pre-GPU, CPU-adjacent):**\n  - **AMX** (Apple Matrix coprocessor, per P-cluster) — accessed via Accelerate (BLAS\n    cblas_sgemm / BNNS), NOT directly (undocumented ISA). Big matmul win vs NEON for the\n    F32/dequantized path. Matmul is the dominant decode cost, so this is the highest-value\n    Apple lever.\n  - **Accelerate / BNNS / vDSP** — Apple's optimized CPU library (uses AMX+NEON). BNNS has\n    quantized ops; vDSP for vector/elementwise.\n  - **ANE (Neural Engine)** — via CoreML; best for a whole-model graph at fp16/int8, harder\n    to use for a custom Q4_K_M kernel (CoreML wants a model graph, limited op flexibility).\n- **GPU / Metal (still PRE-GPU):** MPS / MPSMatrix / MPSGraph. The next tier beyond CPU.\n  Memory rule feedback_gpu_not_a_cpu_lever said \"no GPU unless the user raises\" — the user\n  has now RAISED it as a future lever (not a now-task).\n\nTENSION to resolve before adopting: AMX/Accelerate/ANE are Apple FFI, which conflicts with\nthe HANDOFF's \"pure-Haxe path is the goal, Rust FFI is a reference not the answer\" philosophy.\nAn Apple-accelerated path is the same category as the Rust FFI they moved away from — so\nadopting it is a product/philosophy decision for the user, not a silent optimization. Also\nx86/NUC (the competition target) has no AMX/ANE — an Apple path would be Mac-only, needing a\nportable fallback. Do NOT start any of this without the user explicitly directing it.\n\nCross-platform analog worth noting: x86 has AMX (Intel Advanced Matrix Extensions, distinct\nfrom Apple AMX) on Sapphire Rapids+, but NOT on the i5-1250P NUC target (Alder Lake) — so the\nNUC stays NEON/VNNI-class. See [[project_nuc_x86_target_thermal.md]], [[perf_haxe_kernel_pool_cooperation_blocker.md]].\n\nPrototyped: rayzor-tensors/src/apple_accel.rs (cblas_sgemm nt) + quant.rs amx_prefill_matmul\n(cached Q4-\u003eF32 dequant + sgemm), gated RZT_AMX_PREFILL (default off), Haxe gate in Q4Matmul\n(matmul + matmulFused route prefill batch\u003e=16 through matmulXTQThreaded). Covers 96/112 prefill\nmatmuls (16 skips = Q6_K attn_v/ffn_down). NOT morselized (AMX gate returns before the morsel\npath; gets full batch). **CRITICAL: the FIRST \"AMX net loss\" verdict this session was WRONG —\nmeasured on the ~50% crashing binary (see [[bugs_native_channel_spawned_receiver.md]] tryReceive\nUAF). After the stability fix, clean interleaved ABAB (short prompt, 600-tok gen, TEMP=0, silent):\nAMX OFF ~66.6 tok/s (decode ~69.8) vs AMX ON ~76.5 (decode ~89.0) — AMX WINS EVERY pass, ~15%\ne2e / ~27% decode.** ALWAYS confirm crash-rate=0 before trusting an A/B (this whole reversal was\na crash artifact). PARADOX + LEAD: AMX only runs in prefill (batch\u003e=16) yet speeds up DECODE\n(batch=1, pure Q4-SDOT, never calls AMX). Best hypothesis: the one-time dequant READS every Q4\nweight -\u003e forces all weight pages RESIDENT -\u003e kills recurring mmap page-faults in decode (box has\nform: d66d54d4 preload p99 144-\u003e45ms). If so the decode win is extractable ~FREE via a cheap\nweight pre-fault (madvise/touch), WITHOUT AMX's ~3.3GB F32 dequant — TEST THIS NEXT. Flip side:\nLONG prompt (batch=497) AMX prefill is 1.8x SLOWER (17.4 vs 9.6s SDOT) — sgemm fast (503ms) but\n~8s bleeds into the shared non-matmul path (attention); so AMX is workload-dependent (wins\nshort-prompt/long-gen chat, loses long-prompt/short-gen). Gate should be smarter or fix the\nprefill overhead. Numbers are on a heat-soaked M1 (absolute low); relative ABAB is the signal.\nNUC has no Apple AMX — this is Mac-only; portable path still SDOT/VNNI. Status: UN-PARKED, active.\n\nUser killed F32-for-inference (bench-only). BNNSMatMul probes, correctness-GATED (f32 2x3 PASS\nproves ABI; descriptor: RowMajorMatrix size[0]=cols size[1]=rows stride={1,cols} — value(r,c) at\nc*stride[0]+r*stride[1], docs' reversed convention was the first FAIL): **int8-\u003eint32 and\nint8-\u003ef32 both REJECTED (rc!=0, output untouched) =\u003e Apple's public CPU matmul is FLOAT-ONLY. No\neasy int8-AMX.** NOT signing (adhoc/linker-signed, 0 entitlements, floats pass same process —\nuser asked, verified). Remaining int8 doors, all expensive: deprecated BNNS FC filters (per-tensor\nscale only — cannot represent Q4_K_M per-sub-block scales; exact int8 GEMM needs K-chunk=32 splits\n= 64 API calls/matmul, dead), BNNSGraph (heavy whole-model API), raw undocumented AMX (llama.cpp\nnever shipped AMX int8 either — market signal). **f16 PASSES: 1.0-1.6 TF/s at prefill shapes\n(~1.4-1.6x f32 sgemm), half of F32's dequant/residency (1.65GB)/bandwidth (4x Q4).** GATING FACT\nfor ANY float-GEMM prefill: GEMM rate was never the bottleneck — f32-AMX ran 10x SDOT-effective\nyet LOST e2e (batch=497 ttft 17.4 vs 9.6s, only ~1.05s dequant+sgemm) =\u003e ~16s NON-GEMM bleed on\nthe AMX path, UNEXPLAINED. Root-cause the bleed FIRST (suspects: Accelerate internal threads vs\nSpinPool contention, out-tensor zeros, workspace=null internal allocs); then f16 is the payload\n(500-tok prefill matmul ~9.6s -\u003e ~1s headroom). F32 integration preserved: /tmp/quant.amx-f32-wip.rs\n+ /tmp/Q4Matmul.hx.mine (Haxe gate). Bench: cargo run -p rayzor-tensors --example accel_bench --release.\n\nThe ~16s non-GEMM bleed = the Haxe AMX gate routed EVERY batch\u003e=16 matmul to the Rust kernel,\nincluding Q6_K (attn_v/ffn_down). Runtime's AMX gate AND morsel path both require Q4_K_M -\u003e routed\nQ6_K fell to the LEGACY dequant-per-block fallback: ~700ms/call x 16 = 11.2s (isolated via\nRZT_KERNEL_TIMING atexit dump: matmul fn 12.4s/112 calls vs amx-branch [amx-total] 1.2s; memory\npressure RULED OUT — 0 swaps, 3.8GB RSS on the 16GB box). FIX: gate `qw.scheme() != QScheme.Q6_K`\n(+ anyQ6 skip in matmulFused). RESULT batch=497: ttft 7.6-7.8s vs SDOT 9.8s (~22% WIN, was 1.8x\nloss); 80 routed Q4 calls, 1.2s kernel total. Chat: decode 94-99 vs 68-83 (matmul-path effect),\nttft +~0.6s one-time dequant (first prefill only), output coherent. RZT_AMX_PREFILL still default\nOFF. Instrumentation kept, RZT_AMX_DEBUG-gated ([amx-gate]/[amx-glue]/[amx-total]/[amx-dequant]).\nNEXT = swap cache to f16 (cached f16 weights + f32-\u003ef16 activation convert + BNNSMatMul f16f32,\nprobes PASSED): halves residency 3.3-\u003e1.65GB, sgemm 514ms -\u003e ~350-400ms expected. Sub-detail: the\nRust legacy fallback being 700ms/call for Q6@batch=497 is itself a latent perf bug if anything else\never hits it (Haxe band does the same work in ~1/3 the time); noted, not fixed.\n\namx_prefill_matmul now: cached_f16_weight (Q4 -\u003e f32 staging -\u003e f16 via NEW apple_accel::f32_to_f16\n= vImageConvert_PlanarFtoPlanar16F, chunked 1M elems, correct rounding+subnormals; staging tensor\nFREED; f16 buffer leaked per weight) + per-call activation f32-\u003ef16 into thread-local scratch (~14ms\n@batch=497) + matmul_f16f32_nt (BNNS f16 x f16 -\u003e f32 straight into the out tensor). RESULTS\nbatch=497: ttft 7.09s vs 9.43 SDOT (~25% WIN; f32 variant was 7.6), maxRSS 3.04GB (f32 variant\n3.83), dequant one-time 403ms (was 688), gemm16 497ms (~parity w/ f32 sgemm in-model — probe's\n1.4-1.6x didn't materialize at batch=497, likely SpinPool-idle contention or BNNS workspace=null\nallocs; possible future squeeze, low priority). Chat: ttft tax ~0.8s first-prefill only, decode\nparity-to-better. Coherent. Opt-in RZT_AMX_PREFILL. AMX line now: int8 closed / bleed fixed /\nf16 SHIPPED (opt-in). Remaining AMX ideas: gemm16 in-model rate vs probe gap; BNNSMatMulWorkspaceSize\n+ preallocated workspace; smarter gate (skip AMX below some batch where dequant tax \u003e win);\ndefault-ON decision after NUC-parity thought (Mac-only feature).\n\nWorkspace: BNNSMatMul(workspace=null) allocs internally EVERY call — BNNSMatMulWorkspaceSize +\ngrow-only thread-local buffer =\u003e in-model median 955 -\u003e 1545 GF/s (PROBE-LEVEL; the gap was the\nalloc, not SpinPool contention). AMX f16 prefill now DEFAULT-ON on macOS (RZT_AMX_PREFILL=0/false\nopts out; both gates agree; run_bundle echoes amx_prefill state). batch=497 ttft: 7.02s default vs\n9.49 opted-out (~26%). ROUTE COUNT CORRECTION: 96 Q4 matmuls (not 80) — Q4_K_M promotes\nattn_v/ffn_down to Q6_K on only HALF the layers (8 of 16); the Q4 halves route, Q6 halves stay on\nthe Haxe band. Non-Mac untouched (systemName+cfg gates). AMX line COMPLETE: int8 closed / bleed\nfixed / f16 shipped / workspace squeezed / default-ON. Remaining Apple ideas: BNNSGraph (modern\nAPI), ANE, Metal/MPS (the user's stated big prefill lever).\n\nBNNSGraph is NOT an op-level API: `BNNSGraphCompileFromFile(mlmodelc, function, options)` consumes\na COMPILED COREML MODEL (macOS 15+/iOS 18+; no in-memory graph builder exists). Pipeline: author\n.mlmodel/.mlpackage (mlprogram; coremltools or hand-protobuf) -\u003e `xcrun coremlc compile` (present\nin Xcode) or runtime MLModel.compileModel -\u003e BNNSGraphCompileFromFile -\u003e context/execute. Options\nAPI: single-thread targeting, opt preference, output-path (artifact can be mmap'd cross-process).\nIMPLICATIONS: (1) for the single GEMM it adds a CoreML toolchain for ~no gain — BNNSMatMul (depr\nbut functional) already runs probe-level 1545 GF/s; (2) the REAL play = SUBGRAPH offload (ffn\nblock / whole prefill layer) with Apple's fusion — and the same authored artifact reaches ANE/GPU\nvia CoreML proper = the user's stated big prefill lever; (3) weights must be BAKED into the model\nartifact (per-model-file) or passed as inputs (kills fusion/const-folding). Toolchain on box:\ncoremlc YES (Xcode), coremltools NO (pip venv needed). PROBE PLAN: venv+coremltools -\u003e one-op f16\nmatmul mlpackage (fixed weight) -\u003e coremlc -\u003e Rust FFI (BNNSGraphContextMake/execute — transcribe\nfrom bnns_graph.h) -\u003e measure vs 1545 GF/s baseline; THEN decide subgraph scope.\n\nProbe (rayzor-tensors/examples/bnns_graph_bench.rs + author_*.py; venv coremltools on python3.12 —\n3.14 breaks BlobWriter): ffn_up shape M=497 K=2048 N=8192, fp16 compute. **BNNSGraph baked-weight\n~3.8-3.9 TF/s (2.1x shipped BNNSMatMul 1.8); weights-as-INPUT ~2.8 TF/s with only a 16KB per-SHAPE\nartifact** (rate includes engine-internal f32-\u003ef16 W cast; fp16 io would close toward baked).\nHARD-WON FFI facts (all encoded in the example): _v2 __asm__ renames on\nCompileFromFile/ContextExecute/GetWorkspaceSize (link_name!); handles = {ptr,size} by value; args =\noutputs-first then inputs ALPHABETIZED (GetArgumentPosition = ground truth; 'w'\u003c'x' bit us); model\nio dtype = FLOAT32 (65568) regardless of MIL dtype — coremltools ignored TensorType(fp16) io\nrequest for mb.program (open toolchain detail); silent rc=-1 until\nBNNSGraphContextSetMessageLogCallback wired (gave 'data_ptr_size \u003c expected_footprint').\nCAVEAT: fp16 ACCUMULATION (mean_rel ~1.3% vs f32-accum over K=2048) — model-level quality\nvalidation required before wiring into prefill. INTEGRATION SKETCH (next session): per-shape 16KB\nmlmodelc artifacts (4 shapes) embedded in repo, weights as inputs (f16 io once toolchain detail\nsolved), swap into amx_prefill_matmul behind RZT_AMX_ENGINE=graph; quality gate = llama output\ncomparison vs BNNSMatMul path. Beyond: whole-FFN-block graph (fusion) + ComputeUnit=ALL -\u003e ANE.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_untapped_compute_levers_apple` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}